    "experimental": true,
    "pr_validate": true,
    "note": "Native-HIP AMD (gfx1151) build via the Windows HIP SDK (clang/hipcc, ROCm 6.4 / installer 25.Q3). SCALE, Atlas's other AMD toolchain, is Linux-only, so HIP is the only conceivable Windows AMD path. NOT EXECUTED IN CI: hosted runners have no AMD GPU, so this binary is compiled and packaged but never run \u2014 a green check here means it builds and links, nothing more. The CUDA driver and runtime symbols are satisfied by real HIP-backed shims (crates/atlas-kernels/hip/libcuda_hip_shim.cpp, libcudart_hip_shim.cpp), NOT by stubs; cuBLASLt alone is a deliberate stub (libcublaslt_stub.cpp) that fails its create call, which is safe because the default GEMM path is Atlas's own and cuBLASLt is opt-in via ATLAS_CUBLAS_GEMM=1. Mapping it to hipBLASLt, and porting the spark-storage predictor kernels (its PTX registry is empty on this target), remain open \u2014 see crates/atlas-kernels/hip/README-HIP.md. Running this binary on real gfx1151 hardware additionally needs the Windows runtime fixes in PR #470, which are not merged here yet; without them serve dies at KV sizing because hipMemGetInfo reports no free memory on Windows. Kept experimental so a Windows-clang kernel-compile regression does not block a release.",
    "scale_arch": "gfx1151",
    "target_model": "qwen3.6-27b",
    "target_quant": "nvfp4",
    "test_mode": "no-run"
  }
